<Base title="Privacy and optional analytics" description="How Acquisition Companion handles optional analytics, local progress, search, and AI Deal Lab." type="About"><Crumbs items={[{title:'Privacy'}]}/><article class="narrow"><header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">Your choice</p><h1>Privacy and analytics.</h1></header><div class="prose"><p>Acquisition Companion is free to read without an account. Lesson progress and your analytics choice are saved in this browser. Site search runs locally in your browser.</p><h2 id="ai-deal-lab">Optional AI Deal Lab</h2><p>AI Deal Lab is an optional educational tool. Questions, a short capped conversation context, and the selected synthetic case stage are sent to OpenAI to generate a response. The server sends API requests with <code>store: false</code> and Acquisition Companion does not intentionally maintain a server-side chat history. This setting is not a zero-retention guarantee; OpenAI’s applicable policies may still govern its processing.</p><p>Do not submit confidential, proprietary, personal, or non-public deal information. Version 1 has no private deal-document, CIM, or data-room uploads. Conversation context stays in the active page session and is not saved as a chat history by this site.</p><p>AI Deal Lab analytics events remain subject to the same consent choice as the rest of the site. They may include a selected mode, synthetic case identifier, difficulty, or completion status. Google Analytics does not receive question text, answer text, prompts, response contents, financial figures entered in chat, company names, or conversation transcripts.</p><h2 id="accounts">Optional paid-beta accounts — preparation notice</h2><p>The public course remains free without an account. The Wired Nomad LLC is preparing invite-only Deal Lab subscriptions for U.S. customers; paid access is not yet open. Before launch, the account/privacy terms and retention procedure require review.</p><p>Paid accounts would store your email, an account identifier, hashed sign-in/session credentials, Stripe customer/subscription references and subscription state. Checkout approval records the account identifier, approval/revocation timestamps and operator labels; no identity documents are collected for beta approval. Amazon Web Services SES delivers sign-in email. Stripe provides hosted Checkout and billing management; Acquisition Companion does not collect or store card details.</p><p>Usage accounting records account identifier, timestamp, workflow, model, token counts when supplied, success/failure, latency and estimated cost. It does not store prompts, responses, deal facts or conversation history. Internal cost accounting is not shown in your account. Authentication and billing do not permit private-document uploads.</p><p>Account pages suppress analytics, including sign-in fragments. Other pages retain optional, consent-gated analytics; commercial events use only predefined labels such as billing interval or AI mode, never email, account/customer/subscription identifiers, payment details or chat content. No webhook sends billing information to Google Analytics.</p><p>Sign-in challenges expire after 15 minutes and sessions after seven days; scheduled cleanup removes expired authentication records. Account, billing, approval and usage retention periods, deletion handling, backups and applicable recordkeeping obligations remain legal/operations review items before launch. Usage cleanup is disabled until a reviewed policy explicitly configures it; no general retention period has been chosen. Contact <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a> for account, privacy or deletion requests.</p><h2>Optional Google Analytics</h2><p>If you choose “Allow analytics,” the site loads Google Analytics to understand aggregate site usage. It can record page views, course starts, completed lessons, searches, clicks to original YouTube sources, and non-sensitive AI Deal Lab activity. Search events include the term only when it exactly matches a short list of educational topics; other searches are recorded without the text. We do not send transcript text to Google.</p><p>You can choose “No thanks” and use the entire site. Google Analytics does not load before consent or after a decline. No advertising, remarketing, or advertising personalization is enabled.</p><p>Use <strong>Analytics preferences</strong> in the footer to change your choice. Changing from allow to decline reloads the page to stop the active analytics script. Following an external source link takes you to that site’s own privacy practices.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>For privacy, account or product support, email <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>.</p></div></article></Base>
